   "html_text": "The importance of (CompE) can be illustrated as follows. Consider the case of a father suspected of abusing his child. Suppose that the child does claim that s/he has been abused (label this evidence ⟦M⟧ ). A forensic psychiatrist, when consulted, declares that this confirms guilt ⟦M⟧ . Alternatively, suppose that the child is asked and does not report having been abused ⟦M⟧ As pointed out by Dawes (2001), it may well happen that a forensic psychiatrist will nonetheless interpret this as evidenc",
